DRAI V1 — Dynamic Resonance AI
Self-Organizing Internal Memory for Transformer Models

Production-Ready · Training-Free · Safe on Small Models

DRAI V1 augments transformer attention with a lightweight, stable, self-organizing memory system based on attractor dynamics.
It runs inside the model — no training, no external store, no fine-tuning, no infrastructure — and maintains baseline performance even on small models (70M–410M).

V1 introduces a true internal memory field that emerges through pattern detection and attractor stabilization during generation.
It is safe, deterministic, and specifically engineered not to corrupt the host model.

🔍 What DRAI V1 Does

DRAI V1 extends transformer attention by:

Detecting repeating query patterns over time

Forming attractors for stable, meaningful patterns

Updating attractors via controlled centroid averaging

Decaying and evicting weak attractors

Building a global “memory field vector”

Emitting synthetic multi-head K/V pairs representing learned context

Injecting this memory back into attention in a fully gated, safe way

The result:
A model that can remember, stabilize, and reuse information over the course of a generation.

🚀 Quick Start
from drai import apply_drai_v1
from transformers import AutoModelForCausalLM, AutoTokenizer

model = AutoModelForCausalLM.from_pretrained("EleutherAI/pythia-410m")
model = apply_drai_v1(model)     # Uses V1 conservative config by default

tok = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained("EleutherAI/pythia-410m")
inp = tok("The future of memory systems is", return_tensors="pt")

out = model.generate(inp["input_ids"], max_length=80)
print(tok.decode(out[0]))


Your model now has dynamic, self-organizing memory.

